  "verdict": "The gap is the radome's PEEK column (11.85 mm to the pocket floor) minus the board stack hanging from it, so it moves by 0.28–0.33 µm/K with both together and 0.56 µm/K when the radome leads: over the capsule requirement it closes by up to 20 µm in the cold and opens by 22 µm in the heat (33 / 36 µm with the radome-leads reading). The pins' working stroke follows the gap less the growth of their own brass body (0.031 µm/K, C36000 at 20.5 ppm/K over its 1.49 mm free length): 0.25–0.30 µm/K together, the radome's 0.56 µm/K when it leads. Against 52's L1 (L1 spacer only, ±0.112 mm, which leaves 28 µm to each window edge) the isothermal swing holds the 50–70 % window (margins 8 / 10 µm) and the radome-leads reading breaks it (-8 / -5 µm) — L1 tolerates a radome leading the stack by about 33 K at the extremes, and its isothermal margin reaches zero only for a spacing member of CTE -4.0…-5.6 ppm/K (if the B2B body, not the steel standoff, sets the spacing — its LCP CTE is not in the tree), against 52's RSS residual — a linear sum of the same two terms (±0.15 mm) leaves no room even at the assembly temperature. This is the OUTER pad, with the rim and the stack seated: the centre pad rides on the wire path (HW.34). Daily, 71's capsule (a reading — its error on the range has no known sign) swings by a median 14.5 K and a 95th percentile 24.9 K, a pin stroke of 3.6–13.8 µm — 0.5–2.0 % of the minimum preload once a day — and, if the radome holds the stack in-plane, a pin at radius r slides by 0.95–1.17 µm per mm of r on a 95th-percentile day — 0.06–0.37 µm if the pins follow the board's own in-plane expansion (FR-4 11–15 ppm/K). The thermal swing is added linearly to 52's RSS residual (a systematic term on a statistical one — the conservative stacking), and the one axial term still not computed SHRINKS it — the pocket gasket (placeholder) expands as the PEEK does and pushes the stack the other way — so, for a given temperature field and the seated premises, leaving it out keeps the stroke an upper estimate (the radome-leads reading and 71's daily range are readings, not bounds). Not computed either: the stack's real centring and the centre pad's wire path (HW.34)."
